From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a website frame runs the ad blocker's scriptlets

ChromeContentRendererClient::RunScriptsAtDocumentStart lets a frame's
domicile::CosmeticFilters run the scriptlets the browser sent it, in
the page's world before the page's own scripts and after an Electron
app's preload, and start its procedural filters in their own isolated
world, ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS. See
components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.

Verified: built locally from this series; guard-ad-blocking.sh passes,
its scriptlet and procedural filter checks with it.
---
 chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h         | 4 ++++
 chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h b/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
index d158c41755..09816fe93d 100644
--- a/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
+++ b/chrome/common/chrome_isolated_world_ids.h
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@ enum ChromeIsolatedWorldIDs {
   ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_APPLESCRIPT,
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the ad blocker's procedural filters. See
+  // components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.
+  ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS,
+
   // Numbers for isolated worlds for extensions are set in
   // extensions/renderer/script_injection.cc, and are are greater than or equal
   // to this number.
diff --git a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
index f288108436..549e40160a 100644
--- a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
@@ -1595,6 +1595,11 @@ void ChromeContentRendererClient::RunScriptsAtDocumentStart(
   if (!domicile::ElectronPreload::RunAtDocumentStart(render_frame)) {
     return;
   }
+  // Domicile's engine fork. A website frame's scriptlets, before the page's
+  // own scripts, and its procedural filters, in a world of their own. See
+  // components/domicile/renderer/cosmetic_filters.h.
+  domicile::CosmeticFilters::RunAtDocumentStart(
+      render_frame, ISOLATED_WORLD_ID_DOMICILE_PROCEDURAL_FILTERS);
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_EXTENSIONS_CORE)
   extensions::ExtensionsRendererClient::Get()->RunScriptsAtDocumentStart(
-- 
2.43.0

